PLAN=plan(7,'Lines, angles, triangles and constructions','Part IV · Shape, structure and measure',16,'Orientation in space and time','Space, Measurement','Angle facts, polygon structure and equal-radius constructions let us reason about shapes and check designs before building.','Which triples of lengths can close a triangle, and how can a workshop check a roof design before cutting timber?','In order for a student to think creatively and critically, students must choose an appropriate geometric fact or construction, test a design and explain why the method is reliable.',S,explore,application,assessment,mixed,ready,check,[S[0]['diagram'],S[1]['diagram'],S[2]['diagram'],S[3]['diagram']],['Use angle facts on lines, at points and with parallel lines.','Reason with triangle and polygon angle sums.','Apply the triangle inequality and regular-polygon facts.','Construct perpendicular bisectors, angle bisectors and SSS triangles.'],'acute · right · obtuse · reflex · vertically opposite · corresponding · alternate · co-interior · isosceles · exterior angle · polygon · perpendicular bisector · angle bisector · construction',sourcepages='133–154; answers 229–232')
